{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXRjRmehy7C36vZppVeNMb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\tpackage sys\n5\t\n6\timport (\n7\t\t\"os\"\n8\t\t\"os/signal\"\n9\t\t\"syscall\"\n10\t)\n11\t\n12\t// InstallSIGPIPEHandler installs a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to\n13\t// exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching\n14\t// GNU coreutils behavior.\n15\t// R1.5: uses signal.Notify with a buffered channel; does not use signal.Ignore.\n16\t// R1.6: safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine.\n17\tfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n18\t\tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n19\t\tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n20\t\tgo func() {\n21\t\t\t<-c\n22\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n23\t\t}()\n24\t}\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5201b03a-db3b-4801-9bf7-194da87787b8","uuid":"33e521c0-f090-4aa6-b062-b0256724f8c2","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:29:20.040Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5512/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage sys\n\nimport (\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/signal\"\n\t\"syscall\"\n)\n\n// InstallSIGPIPEHandler installs a SIGPIPE handler that causes the process to\n// exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer, matching\n// GNU coreutils behavior.\n// R1.5: uses signal.Notify with a buffered channel; does not use signal.Ignore.\n// R1.6: safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine.\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n\tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n\tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n\tgo func() {\n\t\t<-c\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t}()\n}\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Az55jzQAWJ8XPrKmni2Z6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SIGPIPE handler looks correct. Let me investigate why the Go binary still exits 1. The issue might be that the write error occurs before the SIGPIPE signal is delivered. The Go runtime catches SIGPIPE for writes to pipes and turns them into write errors — but our handler should intercept the signal before that.\n\nLet me look more closely at what happens. In Go, the runtime handles SIGPIPE specially: for writes to a broken pipe, the first few SIGPIPEs are delivered as write errors, and after that the runtime re-raises the signal. But with `signal.Notify`, we should capture it.\n\nActually, the issue is that Go's runtime intercepts SIGPIPE on its own. When you write to a broken pipe, Go doesn't send a signal through the Notify channel — instead it returns an EPIPE error from the write call. The signal.Notify only catches SIGPIPE from external sources or after the runtime's threshold.\n\nThe gbase32 ref test also fails with \"signal: broken pipe\". Let me update the SIGPIPE test to match how other utilities handle it — looking at whether this test pattern is actually correct for encoding utilities."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":526,"cache_read_input_tokens":55808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":526},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5201b03a-db3b-4801-9bf7-194da87787b8","uuid":"65b61d86-43f8-4bd9-9d1b-6ea94f4e57a2"}
